cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TopoTrail: a QGIS plugin for DEM-based topographic suitability and least-cost route planning"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Luan da Silva Cortes"
    family-names: "Maciel"
    email: "LuanCortesM@users.noreply.github.com"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    affiliation: "Escola Nacional de Botânica Tropical, Instituto de Pesquisas Jardim Botânico do Rio de Janeiro, Brazil"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LuanCortesM/Topotrail"
url: "https://plugins.qgis.org/plugins/TopoTrail/"
abstract: >-
  TopoTrail is a QGIS plugin that supports preliminary planning of trails,
  access routes and field corridors in natural and protected areas. It models
  topographic suitability from a Digital Elevation Model, slope and horizontal
  and vertical curvature using weighted multicriteria analysis, and derives a
  relative topographic risk surface, potential access zones, a least-cost route
  between an origin and a destination, and a metric corridor around that route.
  Results are intended as decision-support evidence and require field
  validation.
keywords:
  - QGIS
  - GIS
  - digital elevation model
  - multicriteria analysis
  - least-cost path
  - trail planning
  - protected areas
  - geomorphometry
license: MIT
version: "0.6.0"
date-released: "2026-09-03"
